From 237a7d080f1ca239921d8b9cc924ee5e62bf044d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:23:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GPU3D: the geometry engine's fast paths (MELONDS_GEOMFAST)

The same work as GPU3D's plain paths, bit for bit: the same vertices, polygons, GXSTAT, FIFO levels and
timing, cycles, matrix reads and test results. MELONDS_GEOMFAST=0 (read as the GPU3D is created) keeps the
plain paths; BananaDS sets it from render.geom_fast (default on).

- Write32 takes the command ports (0x04000440-5CB) first, with CmdFIFOWrite inline and no stack frame, then
  the GX FIFO port (0x04000400-43F, WriteToGXFIFO with CmdFIFOWrite inline); everything else goes to
  Write32Plain, the previous Write32.
- Run is RunFast: ExecuteCommand's body inline in its loop, and in it CmdFIFORead, AddCycles, FinishWork,
  CheckFIFOIRQ (SetIRQ/ClearIRQ and UpdateIRQ for the ARM9) and CheckFIFODMA (NDS::CheckDMAs(0, 7) for the DS's
  four ARM9 DMAs; the DSi's virtual call otherwise). The DMAs aren't looked at while none can wait for the GX
  FIFO: GXFIFODMAMaybe is set by CheckFIFODMA, which DMA::WriteCnt calls when it enables a DMA in that mode (the
  only place StartMode changes), and by Reset and a state load, and cleared when none of the four is in it.
- NEON (GPU3D_NEON.h, with a plain C fallback) for MTX_MULT_4x4/4x3/3x3 and MTX_TRANS, the clip matrix and
  the vertex transform: s32 x s32 -> s64 products (smull/smlal), s64 sums, then >> 12 truncated to 32 bits
  (shrn), as the C code does.
- SubmitPolygon tests the vertices against the view volume first, with ClipAgainstPlane's comparisons, and
  clips only against the planes a vertex is outside of: a pass with no vertex outside its plane only makes the
  colours x.FFF, which they already are (a pass after one that returned 0 still runs). W's size comes from its
  bit length instead of a loop. A strip's two shared vertices keep the previous polygon's Z when both polygons
  use Z-buffering (Z depends on the vertex alone).
- CalculateLighting goes through the enabled lights only.
